The desk merged **412 reports** into #4471 and marked it known: one bug, one fix. The reports
are not one bug. They are three. This page splits them, one ticket each.

## The three problems

| # | problem | reports | tenants | first seen | last seen |
|---|---------|---------|---------|------------|----------|
| 1 | [Parser reads dates month-first for day-first locales](https://github.com/8lueFox/kb-4471-what-it-shows/issues/1) | 374 | 11 | 2026-04-01 | 2026-10-04 |
| 2 | [booking-v3 hints MM/DD/YYYY but reads the date day-first](https://github.com/8lueFox/kb-4471-what-it-shows/issues/2) | 33 | 3 | 2026-04-17 | 2026-09-22 |
| 3 | [One-day moves: off-by-one, not swaps](https://github.com/8lueFox/kb-4471-what-it-shows/issues/3) | 5 | 5 | 2026-04-02 | 2026-06-12 |

374 + 33 + 5 = 412: every report in #4471 has exactly one home.

<Callout kind="warn">
The page for #4471 counts **379** under the parser and footnotes 5 reports "counted where
they're filed". Those 5 are not swaps at all (see problem 3) — the footnote hides a problem,
not a rounding error.
</Callout>

## How to tell them apart

- **Parser** (`src/lib/kb/causes.ts`, `causeOf`): the shared parser reads every date
  month-first. A day-first tenant's dates come out with month and day flipped. Any channel,
  any day-first tenant. This is the bug #4471 was opened for.
- **Hint**: the `booking-v3` form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, people type what
  the hint tells them — month first — and the form then reads it the tenant's way, day-first.
  Same-looking symptom, different bug: only channel `form`, only `booking-v3` tenants
  (alder.physio de-DE, copper.studio es-ES, pale.harbour pt-PT).
- **One-day move**: the date moves by one day, or lands on a different weekday across time
  zones. Bodies say "Tuesday vs Monday", "only June", "Lisbon Tuesday vs Toronto Monday",
  "invite arrived before the booking". No month/day swap anywhere in the text.

## Why the desk saw one problem

- Intake tags disagree with the real cause in 38 of 412 reports: 23 tagged `hint` are
  parser, 15 tagged `parser` are hint. Tag, not tenant+form, drove the merge queue.
- Decision 0001 merges reports on subject lines alone. All of these subjects say the same
  thing ("wrong day", "dates mixed up"), so three bugs merged into one ticket. The decision
  accepted this ("engineering merges them later") — this page is that merge, done.

## What to do

Re-open #4471 into the three tickets above. Until the parser fix ships, the hint bug will
keep producing reports the desk reads as "known" — it is not, and it will not be fixed by
the queued parser fix.

